# Every text file is checked out with LF line ends, on Windows too, whose
# git turns them into CRLF by itself (core.autocrlf): tests compare text
# and scripts run as they are (ADR 0090, decision 9). Git tells binary
# files apart by itself, and leaves them as they are.
* text=auto eol=lf
# But cmd.exe misreads labels in a batch file with LF line ends.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
